config ZART_FIB6
	tristate "zart IPv6 FIB accelerator"
	depends on IPV6
	help
	  Replace IPv6 FIB lookup with zart's fixed 8-bit stride trie.
	  Provides 3.75x faster longest-prefix-match for IPv6 routing.

	  zart resolves IPv6 LPM in exactly 16 memory accesses,
	  compared to the kernel's fib6 tree walk which can require
	  up to 128 node traversals for long prefixes.

	  If unsure, say N.
